# Command mpv

## What does this command do:

Command line media player

## Installed from

For Fedora install using: sudo dnf install -y mpv
For Raspberry Pi install using: sudo apt install -y mpv
For Mac install using: brew install mpv
For Mac container (Fedora Linux, ARM/aarch64) install using: sudo dnf install -y mpv

## Command path

For Fedora run: /usr/bin/mpv
For Raspberry Pi run: /usr/bin/mpv
For Mac run: /opt/homebrew/bin/mpv
For Mac container run: /usr/bin/mpv

## Command documentation

Docs can be found at https://github.com/mpv-player/mpv

## Command options

# Play a file
mpv <file>

# Play a URL (YouTube, etc. via yt-dlp)
mpv <url>

# Start at a specific time position
mpv --start=<time> <file>          # time as seconds, hh:mm:ss, or percent

# Fullscreen
mpv --fs <file>

# Audio only (no video window)
mpv --no-video <file>

# Video only (no audio)
mpv --no-audio <file>

# Load a subtitle file
mpv --sub-file=<subtitle.srt> <file>

# Play a playlist file
mpv --playlist=<playlist.m3u>

# Loop playback
mpv --loop <file>
mpv --loop-playlist <playlist>

# Set volume (0-100, default 100; can exceed 100)
mpv --volume=<0-130> <file>

# List all available options
mpv --list-options

# Search options by keyword
mpv --h=<string>

# Interactive keyboard shortcuts (during playback)
# q / Q       quit / quit and save position
# space       pause/unpause
# f           toggle fullscreen
# m           mute
# 9 / 0       decrease / increase volume
# [ / ]       decrease / increase playback speed
# , / .       step backward / forward one frame
# left/right  seek ±5 seconds
# up/down     seek ±60 seconds
# s           screenshot
# i           show file info overlay
